Communication
What method/channel will your team use to communicate?
Our team will communicate mainly through discord or email.

What is the agreed upon maximum time limit for responding to a team communication?
Members are expected to respond to messages within a day maximum, or ideally within a few hours (4-5) after a message has been sent and addressed towards any team members.

If a team member believes they may not be able to complete a task by a deadline, what is the timeline and method for informing the team?
If a team member is unable to complete a section of their assigned part for any reason, they are expected to notify the team either through discord or email at least one day previous of the deadline. If a team member expects themselves to be unable to complete a specific assignment until a certain day for any reason, they should notify the team immediately. 
Suggested Process for Addressing Problems
Step 1: Address the situation directly
Adhering to your team's list of expected behaviours, give constructive feedback. 
	Example: We agreed that… but we’re not seeing…

	Separate facts from interpretations:
		Fact: We’ve noticed that…
		Interpretation: This makes it seem like…
Step 2: Provide a first notice, in writing
Be clear about the amount of time you will give your teammates to respond, turn in missing/late work, show up for class, or demonstrate a change in behaviour.
Step 3: Provide a second notice, in writing, copying your instructor
Decide on the amount of time allowed to respond and make changes.
Step 4: Provide a final notice, in writing, copying your instructor
State the consequence if the issue is not resolved in “X” amount of time.
Removing a member from the team
Under what circumstances would you request that your instructor remove someone from the team? 
🚩 It is expected that the team member has been informed ahead of time that their behaviour is not acceptable and given a chance to improve (e.g., constructive conversations and written notices).
